{
    "name": "E2E Shopify - Return Tracking Trigger",
    "description": "Return Tracking fires on return events of a fulfilled order (manual step).",
    "notes": {
        "9087035e-180d-4604-a704-05f830abac65": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": -128,
            "width": 400,
            "height": 400,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Manual E2E — requires a return on a fulfilled order\n\nThe trigger listens to every `returns/*` topic. A return needs a **fulfilled order**, and creating one through the API needs the `write_returns` scope, which the connector does not request (the QA app does not have it either — `returnRequest` answers ACCESS_DENIED).\n\n### How to test\n1. Start this flow (the webhooks are registered on start).\n2. In the Shopify admin open **Orders** → a fulfilled order → **Return** → select the items and a reason → **Create return** (fires `returns/request` or `returns/approve`).\n3. With `write_returns` granted, the GraphQL Admin API works too: `returnRequest` (`returns/request`) → `returnApproveRequest` (`returns/approve`) → `returnClose` (`returns/close`), using the order's `fulfillmentLineItemId`.\n\nThe Assert checks the return id, its order and that the topic starts with `returns/`. AfterAll timeout is 300 s — create the return within 5 minutes of starting the flow. `returns/update` alone never fires during a standard return journey."
        }
    },
